<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} schema={schema}><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'Compare',href:'/compare/'},{label:'Systeme.io vs ClickFunnels'}]}/><article><header class="section"><div class="container"><h1>Systeme.io vs ClickFunnels: Compare the Stack, Not Two Entry Prices</h1><p class="lede">Both can run funnels, email and digital products. Their pricing architecture is radically different.</p></div></header><div class="narrow prose article-body"><AffiliateDisclosure hasRelationship={true}/><p>ClickFunnels Launch is $97/month and includes 10,000 contacts, 50,000 emails/month, three courses, three communities, five custom domains and one workspace. Scale is $197 and Optimize $297. Systeme.io's primary pricing page lists Free, $17, $47 and $97 tiers.</p><h2>What the price gap does—and does not—prove</h2><p>It proves Systeme.io has a much lower entry cost. It does not prove a $17 plan is equivalent to every ClickFunnels workflow. Contacts, funnels, automations, courses and operational limits must be compared at the plan each business actually requires.</p><h2>Choose Systeme.io when</h2><p>You want an integrated funnel/email/course stack and software cost is a major constraint. Its Free plan also makes it possible to validate a small workflow before committing to a paid subscription.</p><h2>Choose ClickFunnels when</h2><p>Your business is already organized around ClickFunnels' funnel ecosystem, workspace model and included capacity, and migration cost or workflow disruption outweighs subscription savings.</p><h2>Verdict</h2><p>Systeme.io has the stronger value case for many small operators. ClickFunnels should be judged against the cost of replacing the complete workflow, not against Systeme.io's cheapest headline price.</p><p><a class="button" href={aff} rel="sponsored nofollow">Try Systeme.io free</a></p><SourceBlock sources={sources}/><p class="source-note">Pricing checked September 10, 2026. This comparison does not claim hands-on conversion or UX superiority.</p></div></article></BaseLayout>